# Canonicalization

Environment: NixOS with preservation. HOME is a local-only Git repository with a whitelist .gitignore that tracks persistent state and contains flake-enabled Git submodules in Go-style paths. Each submodule follows a subset of the numtide/blueprint directory structure.

Run `git_canonicalization help` for the action guide and
`git_canonicalization help COMMAND` for command-specific instructions.

## Development rules

Use native Git commands for repository lifecycle operations.
Use `git_canonicalization` for persistent directory-structure changes and preserve its strict canonical layout.
Put deliberate opaque persistent exceptions under `prm/` and generated artifacts under `tmp/`.
After making changes, run `nix fmt` and `nix flake check`.
